{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.CategoricalMassMarkov","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.CategoricalMassMarkov","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LinearIndependent.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.term_one_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.term_one_unit","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-mass-markov.lean#L98-L102","doc":"Unit witness: the unit `1 ∈ A` has `tr_M = 1`, so its\nTerm-1 contribution is `|1| = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.term_one_descends","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.term_one_descends","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-mass-markov.lean#L83-L96","doc":"**Non-trivial descent property of Term 1.**\n\nTerm 1 is invariant under shifts by elements of the confinement\nideal J1: adding any `j ∈ J1` to T_w does not change the\nTerm-1 value.  This is the spectral-sequence reading\n`Term 1 = ⟨tr_M, E_∞^{0,*}⟩`: only the J1-quotient class of\nT_w contributes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.term_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.term_one","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-mass-markov.lean#L79-L81","doc":"**Term 1 of the unified mass formula** is the descended-trace\nabsolute value `|tr_M T_w|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.markov_descends","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.markov_descends","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-mass-markov.lean#L66-L77","doc":"**Markov trace descends through the confinement quotient.**\n\n`tr_M` factors through `A / J^1`, i.e. it depends only on the\nimage in the descended quotient.  This is the Lean shadow of\nthe spectral-sequence statement\n`tr_M = ⟨tr_M, E_∞^{0,*}⟩`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.tr_M_vanishes_on_J1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.tr_M_vanishes_on_J1","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-mass-markov.lean#L60-L60","doc":"Trace vanishes on the confinement ideal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.tr_M_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.tr_M_one","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-mass-markov.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Markov trace of the unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.one","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-mass-markov.lean#L56-L56","doc":"Identity element (the `[1]` class). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.J1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.J1","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-mass-markov.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The GB-filtration submodule `J^1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.tr_M","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.tr_M","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-mass-markov.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The Markov trace, an ℝ-linear functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-mass-markov.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra","kind":"class","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-mass-markov.lean#L46-L60","doc":"Abstract Hecke-style algebra carrying a Markov trace and a\nconfinement filtration ideal `J1` whose elements have zero\nMarkov trace.  This is the minimal structural data for\nTerm 1 of the mass formula. ","signatureChunk":0}]}